  },
  {
   "index": 6,
   "tag": "p×3",
   "landmarks": [
    "article",
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 679,
   "text": "Today I was running a query (using SQLite’s FTS5 for\nfull-text search) on a table with 4000 rows and it took 5 seconds. That seemed\nwrong to me: computers are fast!\nIt turned out that what I needed to do was to run ANALYZE!\nImmediately the problem query went from taking 5 seconds to like 0.05 seconds\n(or some other number small enough that I didn’t care to investigate further).\nI still don’t know ",
   "counts": {
    "links": 3,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 3,
    "repeats": 3,
    "coverLinks": 0
