    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 8,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "article",
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 204,
   "text": "Occasionally I’ve run into situations where I accidentally put a bunch of rows\nin my database that I don’t want to be there (for example completed tasks from\ndjango-tasks-db), and I want to clean them up.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.07,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 982,
    "height": 60,
    "widthFraction": 0.4,
    "leftFraction": 0.3,
    "pageFraction": 0.32,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 9,
   "tag": "ol",
   "landmarks": [
    "article",
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 567,
   "text": "What’s happened to me a few times in this case is:\nI run some kind of command to clean up the rows\nThe command takes more than 5 seconds, since there are a lot of rows (though I still have some questions about why these DELETE statements are so slow honestly, maybe there’s a bunch of Python code running inside a transaction, I’m not sure)\nOne of the other workers tries to write the database while ",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 4,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1054,
    "height": 236,
